From: Kestrel OS port <local>
Subject: [PATCH, DIAGNOSTIC, LOCAL-ONLY] disable five tail NoCs on Slim 3

Rationale: native boot resets silently right after the 1770000/1780000
interconnect probes in every config; the only qnoc nodes left untested
are gem/nsp/lpass-ag/lpiaon/lpicx. Single-variable-group test whether
a late qnoc probe is the reset site. NOT for publication or general
ARM64 support.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x126100-lenovo-ideapad-slim3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x126100-lenovo-ideapad-slim3.dts
@@ -1682,3 +1682,15 @@
 &pcie_south_anoc {
 	status = "disabled";
 };
+
+/* DIAGNOSTIC 2026-10-11 (0007): disable the five tail NoCs (gem, nsp,
+ * lpass ag/lpiaon/lpicx) to test whether a late qnoc probe is the
+ * silent-reset site observed after the 1770000/1780000 probes.
+ * Local-only experiment, not for publication. */
+&gem_noc { status = "disabled"; };
+&nsp_noc { status = "disabled"; };
+&lpass_ag_noc { status = "disabled"; };
+&lpass_lpiaon_noc { status = "disabled"; };
+&lpass_lpicx_noc { status = "disabled"; };
